<title>SRI LANKA: Commercial Bank up 3.5 pct on results.</title>
<headline>Commercial Bank up 3.5 pct on results.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Sri Lanka's Commercial Bank Ltd rose 3.52 percent or five rupees to 147 in early Monday trade on higher 1996 results, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The price is reacting mainly to good profit figures,&quot; said a trader at Ceylinco Stock Brokers.</p>
<p>Commercial Bank reported a net profit of 433.36 million rupees for the year to December 31, 1996, up 31.7 percent against 329.03 million rupees in the previous year.</p>
<p>Commercial Bank is one of four private commercial banks listed in Colombo.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
